<http://data.silknow.org/object/e8679616-b83b-3f17-a20a-262191eb44a7>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Due to its relatively flat surface, this densely-worked Venetian needle lace is known as point plat. Point plat was believed to have developed as a slightly less time-consuming version of the three-dimensional Venetian needle lace gros point. This particular piece was rearranged into a chalice veil as part of a set of church vestments. This is part of the set 10.186.1, .2, .3, .5 that comprises a chasuble, maniple, stole, and chalice veil."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/b977f454-7ce6-3597-981b-3db92f5d52b0> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/c7c61532-3688-3897-948c-ea6f93eecdef> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Due to its relatively flat surface, this densely-worked Venetian needle lace is known as point plat. Point plat was believed to have developed as a slightly less time-consuming version of the three-dimensional Venetian needle lace gros point. This particular piece was rearranged into a chalice veil as part of a set of church vestments. This is part of the set 10.186.1, .2, .3, .5 that comprises a chasuble, maniple, stole, and chalice veil."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/e8679616-b83b-3f17-a20a-262191eb44a7/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/e8679616-b83b-3f17-a20a-262191eb44a7/dimension/1> ;
